                                "target_word": "Virginia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e99f9ad-c1df-3db0-8639-8e9e30a994d5",
                                        "entry_id": "7866081b-9d81-3cae-bdce-2cfe4aafa944",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of the United States. Official name: Commonwealth of Virginia. Capital: Richmond."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6393bb8-4bb3-4c41-ad94-8c63d6441645",
                                                "sense_id": "8e99f9ad-c1df-3db0-8639-8e9e30a994d5",
                                                "text": "We, whose names are underwritten, the loyall Subjects of our dread Soveraigne Lord King James, by the Grace of God, of Great Britaine, France, and Ireland, King, Defender of the Faith, &c. Having undertaken for the glorie of God, and advancement of the Christian faith, and the honor of our King and Country, a Voyage to plant the first Colonie in the Northerne parts of Virginia; doe by these Presents, solemnly and mutually, in the Presence of God and one another, covenant and combine ourselves together into a civill Body politike, for our better ordering and preservation, and furtherance of the ends aforesaid:[...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7af24078-5ec6-4ddd-bf1c-559cb9c6c275",
                                                "sense_id": "8e99f9ad-c1df-3db0-8639-8e9e30a994d5",
                                                "text": "And on March 21, Virginia passed a law banning colorants from school food, effective July 1, 2027."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b28210c8-6775-4538-a2ae-b526ddbad11b",
                                                "sense_id": "8e99f9ad-c1df-3db0-8639-8e9e30a994d5",
                                                "text": "Resendiz was last seen on May 29 in her barracks in Miller Hall at Naval Station Norfolk, according to a missing person’s alert issued by Virginia State Police on June 3."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "42e4c8ca-31e9-3133-b9ba-b16d6871723c",
                                        "entry_id": "7866081b-9d81-3cae-bdce-2cfe4aafa944",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A former colony that was a part of the British Empire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "32ae5c09-4ffd-3bca-9a06-7e6f0900048e",
                                        "entry_id": "7866081b-9d81-3cae-bdce-2cfe4aafa944",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "50 Virginia, a main belt asteroid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5bfda9e-3982-3497-91b9-ce997af21479",
                                        "entry_id": "7866081b-9d81-3cae-bdce-2cfe4aafa944",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female given name from Latin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ce2b7d8-3f80-46bd-97ea-57739f9c0b8f",
                                                "sense_id": "c5bfda9e-3982-3497-91b9-ce997af21479",
                                                "text": "1380s-1390s, Geoffrey Chaucer, The Canterbury Tales: The Physician's Tale\n\"Daughter,\" quoth he, \"Virginia by thy name, / There be two wayes, either death or shame, / That thou must suffer, - alas that I was bore!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2634cdf-acc8-4e26-958e-b28d2ffc068f",
                                                "sense_id": "c5bfda9e-3982-3497-91b9-ce997af21479",
                                                "text": "Here, in due time, she was brought to bed of a daughter, whom she christened by the name of Virginia; not so much out of respect to her last mistress, who bore that name, as because she considered it peculiarly ladylike and genteel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9570003a-d1ea-49c6-b2fc-c8ad98f0bcfd",
                                                "sense_id": "c5bfda9e-3982-3497-91b9-ce997af21479",
                                                "text": "O sweet Virginia Dare! / Thou art the lily of our love, / The forest's sylph-like queen, / The first-born bud from Saxon stem / That this New World hath seen!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa4ae327-f07d-48b1-87c8-f4e07ed785e2",
                                                "sense_id": "c5bfda9e-3982-3497-91b9-ce997af21479",
                                                "text": "She said her name was Virginia Severson. It suited her. She looked very virginal, and clean, calm, cool in a Scandinavian sort of way."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfe77132-b596-4022-91c5-c0973962ae8e",
                                                "sense_id": "c5bfda9e-3982-3497-91b9-ce997af21479",
                                                "text": "The city of Waukesha confirmed the names of five victims as Virginia Sorenson, 79; Leanna Owen, 71; Tamara Durand, 52; Jane Kulich, 52; and Wilhelm Hospel, 81."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
